### Orvexa API v1 — journey step 04: interaction lifecycle
### Open an interaction (auto-opens the customer's open conversation for the
### channel when conversation_id is omitted), walk the guarded lifecycle
### (pending → active → wrapup → completed|failed|canceled; illegal → 409),
### assign agent/queue.
###
### Wire contract (issue #101): request and response keys are the snake_case
### names documented by api/openapi/orvexa-v1.yaml — `customer_id`,
### `conversation_id`, `provider_ref`, `idempotency_key` in, `id`, `status`, …
### out.

@ORVEXA_URL = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_URL}}
@ORVEXA_KEY = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_KEY}}

### Create an inbound chat interaction → 201 (captures id)
# inbound + no conversation_id → find-or-open the customer's open conversation
# @name createInteraction
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/interactions
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "{{createCustomer.response.body.$.data.id}}",
  "channel": "chat",
  "direction": "inbound",
  "source": "web",
  "destination": "support",
  "provider": "internal",
  "idempotency_key": "d9-chat-0001"
}

###

### Get the interaction → 200
# @name getInteraction
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/interactions/{{createInteraction.response.body.$.data.id}}
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}

###

### Guarded transition: pending → active → 200
# to ∈ pending|active|wrapup|completed|failed|canceled (illegal → 409 with
# error.details.allowed)
# @name transitionActive
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/interactions/{{createInteraction.response.body.$.data.id}}/transition
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "active"
}

###

### Assign the agent (agent_id/queue_id both optional) → 200
# @name assignInteraction
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/interactions/{{createInteraction.response.body.$.data.id}}/assign
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent_id": "{{registerAgent.response.body.$.data.id}}"
}
